nodecode-priors is a rewrite of priors-agents's priors-agents/priors:

  https://github.com/priors-agents/priors
  commit 17d3e1fd9b4348bb8baf1e3983d14d07dedd39c5
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Priors contributors (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the Hermes plugin at integrations/hermes, which declared
two MCP servers -- the hosted read-only one at https://mcp.priors.trade/mcp
and the local `priors-mcp` command -- plus one skill. This cell speaks both
MCP wires in Common Lisp: streamable HTTP (initialize, the
Mcp-Session-Id header, JSON or SSE bodies) for the hosted server's seven
read tools, and JSON-RPC over a child command's stdin for the wallet's five
(credit_status, wallet_balance, pay_url, borrow, repay), passing the
command the same PRIORS_* environment the plugin's mcp.json declared. The
skill became (help :priors), the manual topic the model reads. The tool
names keep their server-side spelling, prefixed priors_.

What was left out and why: the plugin's install-time wiring -- npm, Hermes's
plugin catalog, and the `trust: untrusted` approval that asked the user
before every write. None of it exists in a cell. The command is instead the
user's own (the section names it, default priors-mcp), and the approval is
the section's bounds: pay_hosts, max_price_usd, and what the model
confirms. The harness's own per-call prompt has no counterpart here, which
the README says plainly. Also left out: the long-lived wallet server, which
a cell cannot own, so each wallet call is one child run; and the plugin's
demo, tests and release plumbing, which belong to the original repository.
